# Line endings.
#
# This matters more than usual here: several files are verified byte-for-byte against a
# SHA-256 recorded in a manifest. If Git rewrites their line endings on checkout, the
# checksum no longer matches and the application refuses to load them — which is exactly
# what happened before this file existed. OCR failed outright on Windows checkouts, and
# `scripts\build_windows.ps1` failed its release gate, because `core.autocrlf` had
# converted every LF in `inference.yml` and `dictionary.txt` to CRLF.

# Store text as LF in the repository and check it out as LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch and PowerShell scripts need CRLF in the working tree.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Checksum-verified assets: never transform these, in either direction.
resources/ocr/ppocrv6/** -text
resources/moj/trust-anchors/** -text
docs/external/moj/certs/** -text

# Byte-exact expected output for the fixed copy-text contract.
tests/fixtures/text_export/*.txt -text

# Binary formats.
*.onnx binary
*.zip  binary
*.crt  binary
*.ico  binary
*.png  binary
*.pdf  binary
